## Context
Child of tracker 1317 (forge leaks). Status and hygiene scripts that list or view requests with
raw `gh`; on a no-forge repository they fail or report an empty list as "no open requests".
Builds on the forge.py CLI shape set by 1318.

Sites on main 2026-10-28:
- `skills/dashboard/dashboard.sh` (~25-28: open and recently merged PR lists)
- `scripts/raid-sitrep.py` (~45: open PR list). A sibling raid edits raid files: before
  touching it, check no open PR edits it (`gh pr list --json number,files`).
- `scripts/slow_tickets.py` (~82: PR view createdAt, mergedAt, comments, checks)
- `scripts/project-state.py` (~397), `scripts/tmp_report.py` (~717),
  `scripts/worktree-tmp-guard.py` (~206): PR lists found by the 1317 filing sweep, not in the
  tracker's original list.

Parent: tracker 1317.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The six sites above call `forge.py` instead of `gh`, or are listed in this ticket's log as
      residue with a reason; on the none backend a listing answers from refs/notes/review or a
      typed NOOP, never an empty list read as "nothing open"
- [ ] Each ported site has a `none`-backend test (no `gh` on PATH) showing the step still
      works or answers a typed NOOP/refusal, never an empty all-clear
- [ ] A verb or CLI subcommand is added to `scripts/forge.py` only where a caller here needs it,
      with its gh and none behaviour tested in `tests/test_forge.py`
- [ ] `make check` passes
